Research references (architectures adapted in original code; no implementation copied):
- Kingma, Welling. Auto-Encoding Variational Bayes. https://arxiv.org/abs/1312.6114
- Kipf, Welling. Variational Graph Auto-Encoders. https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.07308
The graph module adds a feature-conditioned learned Gaussian prior; it is not an
exact reproduction of the cited standard-normal-prior VGAE.

Models / data:
- No third-party pretrained weights, customer datasets, LLMs or paid APIs.
- Bundled demo weights were trained locally on the included fictional simulator.
- The attached hackathon brief informed the schema; the brief is not redistributed.

Modeled integrations:
- FNS_MOCK: always confirms a synthetic company is registered.
- BKI_MOCK: returns generated debt and overdue values; no bureau is contacted.
- Document bodies are synthetic text records, not signed files or OCR outputs.
- Signing and disbursement are state events and loan rows only; no real transfers.
- Product names, rates and credit rules are fictional demo configuration.
